 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Ear and Ease, as if the couch were heaven,\nCall me of earth to welcome my spirit,\nAnd that I be mine; but never again\nThis first, this last solitude admit.\nBut when in hours like these, alone,\nMy soul's likeness dies on earth too early,\nI feel it with a greater sorrow,\nThough its price should be infinitely dear.\nYou are so lovely now! You have forgotten\nWhy you sit at my feet in earthly love.\nWhat can it cost me now to forget\nAll things which e'er our happiness have?",
